      "overview": "All protocol types follow a uniform code-generated binary serialization pattern using Netty ByteBuf. Types have a fixed-size block (containing primitive and fixed-size struct fields) followed by a variable-size block (for strings, arrays, maps, and variable-sized nested structs). Nullable fields use bit-field bytes at the start. Variable fields use 4-byte LE offset slots pointing into the variable block. Polymorphic types use VarInt type-ID prefix for deserialization dispatch.",
      "patterns": [
