          "name": "Fixed+Variable Block Layout",
          "description": "Each type declares NULLABLE_BIT_FIELD_SIZE, FIXED_BLOCK_SIZE, VARIABLE_FIELD_COUNT, VARIABLE_BLOCK_START, MAX_SIZE. The binary layout is: [null-bits] [fixed fields] [variable offset slots (4 bytes each)] [variable data]. Variable offset slots store relative offsets from the variable block start; -1 means null.",
          "examples": ["AmbienceFX: 1 null byte + 18 fixed bytes + 6x4 offset slots = 42 bytes before variable data"]
        },
        {
          "name": "Null Bit Fields",
          "description": "First N bytes are null-bit fields. Each bit indicates whether a nullable field is present. Bit ordering is LSB-first within each byte.",
          "examples": ["AmbienceFXConditions uses 2 null-bit bytes for 10 nullable fields"]
        },
        {
          "name": "VarInt Length-Prefixed Arrays",
          "description": "Arrays are serialized as VarInt count followed by elements. Fixed-size elements are packed contiguously; variable-size elements use per-element computeBytesConsumed. Max array length is typically 4,096,000.",
          "examples": ["AbilityEffects.disabled: VarInt count + InteractionType bytes"]
        },
        {
          "name": "VarInt-Prefixed Strings",
          "description": "Strings use PacketIO.readVarString/writeVarString: VarInt byte-length prefix + UTF-8 bytes. Max string length is typically 4,096,000 bytes.",
          "examples": ["Asset.hash uses fixed 64-byte encoding, but most strings use VarInt prefix"]
        },
        {
          "name": "Polymorphic Type-ID Dispatch",
          "description": "Abstract types (ComponentUpdate, Interaction, Selector, ParamValue) use VarInt type-ID at the start of serialized data. Deserialization reads the type-ID and dispatches to the concrete subtype's deserialize method.",
          "examples": ["ComponentUpdate: typeId 0=Nameplate, 5=Item, 6=Block, etc."]
        },
        {
          "name": "Dictionary/Map Serialization",
          "description": "Maps are serialized as VarInt count + key-value pairs. Keys are typically enum values (1 byte) and values are either primitives or nested structs.",
          "examples": ["InteractionConfiguration.useDistance: Map<GameMode, Float>", "InteractionConfiguration.priorities: Map<InteractionType, InteractionPriority>"]
        },
        {
          "name": "Bitfield-Encoded String Arrays",
          "description": "Some nullable-element string arrays (like activeAnimations) use a bitfield to indicate which elements are non-null, followed by the non-null strings.",
          "examples": ["ActiveAnimationsUpdate.activeAnimations"]
